---An object representing the certificate-authority-data for your cluster.
---@class aws.eks.Certificate
---@field data? aws.eks.String The Base64-encoded certificate data required to communicate with your cluster. Add this to the certificate-authority-data section of the kubeconfig file for your cluster.
---@field active? aws.eks.ActiveCertificateAuthority An object identifying the certificate authority that is currently signing certificates for the cluster.

---An object representing a certificate authority (CA) for an Amazon EKS cluster.
---@class aws.eks.CertificateAuthority
---@field id? aws.eks.String The unique identifier of the certificate authority.
---@field createdAt? aws.eks.Timestamp The Unix epoch timestamp in seconds for when the certificate authority was created.
---@field createdBy? aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityCreatedBy The entity that created the certificate authority. Certificate authorities that you create are CUSTOMER; those that Amazon EKS provisions on your behalf, such as a cluster's initial certificate authority, are EKS.
---@field activatedAt? aws.eks.Timestamp The Unix epoch timestamp in seconds for when the certificate authority was last activated as the cluster's signer. This value is absent if the certificate authority has never been activated.
---@field activatedBy? aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityActivatedBy The entity that most recently activated the certificate authority. A value of EKS indicates that Amazon EKS activated it automatically; CUSTOMER indicates that you activated it.
---@field signingStatus? aws.eks.CertificateAuthoritySigningStatus The signing status of the certificate authority. IN_USE means the certificate authority is currently signing certificates for the cluster, ACTIVATING means it's being promoted to the signer, and NOT_USED means it's trusted by the cluster (for example, a successor CA during a rotation, or a retired outgoing CA) but isn't the signer.
---@field distributionStatus? aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityDistributionStatus The distribution status of the certificate authority, which tracks whether Amazon EKS has distributed its trust to the Amazon Web Services managed components in your cluster (the control plane, Amazon EKS Auto Mode instances, and Amazon Web Services Fargate nodes). Valid values are IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETE, FAILED, and DELETING. A successor CA can only be activated after its distribution status is CO...
---@field validity? aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityValidity The validity period of the certificate authority's certificate.
---@field scheduledEvents? aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityScheduledEvents The scheduled auto-activation events for the certificate authority, computed from its validity period.
---@field rollbackAvailable? aws.eks.BoxedBoolean Indicates whether CA rollback is still available for this certificate authority. After you activate a successor CA, rollback lets you revert to the outgoing CA for a limited period while you finish updating any worker nodes or clients that were missed.
---@field data? aws.eks.String The Base64-encoded public certificate of the certificate authority.

---@alias aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityActivatedBy "EKS"|"CUSTOMER"

---@alias aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityCreatedBy "EKS"|"CUSTOMER"

---@alias aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityDistributionStatus "IN_PROGRESS"|"COMPLETE"|"FAILED"|"DELETING"

---@alias aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityMaxResults number

---The scheduled events during which Amazon EKS may automatically activate a certificate authority, computed from its validity period. These events help ensure that a cluster's signing certificate authority is rotated before its certificate expires.
---@class aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityScheduledEvents
---@field firstAutoActivation? aws.eks.Timestamp The earliest Unix epoch timestamp in seconds at which Amazon EKS may automatically activate this certificate authority.
---@field finalAutoActivation? aws.eks.Timestamp The Unix epoch timestamp in seconds by which Amazon EKS will automatically activate this certificate authority if you haven't already activated it.

---@alias aws.eks.CertificateAuthoritySigningStatus "NOT_USED"|"ACTIVATING"|"IN_USE"

---Summary information about a certificate authority (CA) for an Amazon EKS cluster, returned by ListCertificateAuthorities and the certificate-authority write operations.
---@class aws.eks.CertificateAuthoritySummary
---@field id? aws.eks.String The unique identifier of the certificate authority.
---@field createdAt? aws.eks.Timestamp The Unix epoch timestamp in seconds for when the certificate authority was created.
---@field createdBy? aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityCreatedBy The entity that created the certificate authority, either CUSTOMER or EKS.
---@field activatedAt? aws.eks.Timestamp The Unix epoch timestamp in seconds for when the certificate authority was last activated. This value is absent if the certificate authority has never been activated.
---@field activatedBy? aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityActivatedBy The entity that most recently activated the certificate authority, either CUSTOMER or EKS.
---@field signingStatus? aws.eks.CertificateAuthoritySigningStatus The signing status of the certificate authority: IN_USE, ACTIVATING, or NOT_USED.
---@field distributionStatus? aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityDistributionStatus The distribution status of the certificate authority: IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETE, FAILED, or DELETING.

---@alias aws.eks.CertificateAuthoritySummaryList aws.eks.CertificateAuthoritySummary[]

---The validity period of a certificate authority's certificate.
---@class aws.eks.CertificateAuthorityValidity
---@field notBefore? aws.eks.Timestamp The Unix epoch timestamp in seconds for the start of the certificate authority's validity period.
---@field notAfter? aws.eks.Timestamp The Unix epoch timestamp in seconds for the end of the certificate authority's validity period.

